  "rp_wiring_revision": "2026-11-06",
  "status": "Gowin-built 50.4 MHz GPU-video board image with 2 us GPIO host phases; the GPU terminal runs on HDMI with keyboard input after the firmware stack fix (user-reported 2026-11-07). PIO/DMA, NARM integration and external electrical qualification remain unresolved.",
  "firmware_modified": true,
  "firmware_source": "https://github.com/apc53pro/MPC-2350/commit/cb2eb28",
  "rtl_modified": true,
  "modification_flags_scope": "MPC-2350 host bus at 2 us phases (first proven at 50 us); board image back to the 50.4 MHz GPU-video profile, built with Gowin EDA under the AGENTS.md exception. Pin mappings and packet ABI are unchanged.",
  "hardware_tested": false,
  "hardware_observation": "Before the 6.3 MHz bus-test build, user reports monitor lock to black with GPU_RESET_N HIGH and matching RP address-pad echoes. Earlier status/capability reads returned all FF and then all zero. Both separate 4.7 kohm handshake pull-downs are fitted. The subsequent 6.3 MHz core / 50 us host-phase build still returned sixteen zero capability bytes; slowing the clocks did not change readback. Printing all sixteen bytes means software sampled WREADY and RVALID HIGH during transfers; their later idle LOW levels do not describe active transfers. Early capability failure leaves GPU BOOT zero-initialized and unread. All eight data-wire continuities were checked. On 2026-11-06, a held read of register 0x41 measured RVALID pin 74 at 3.3 V, WREADY pin 73 at 0 V, RD_N pin 16 at 0.23 V and all eight Tang data pins at 0 V (expected D1 pin 28 HIGH); swap-test edges were 1 1 1 1, indicating, without isolating the cause, that the FPGA latched a different capability-range address. Cold power-up first read all FF before FPGA configuration completed. Terminal/bus operation and electrical qualification remain unresolved; hardware_tested is false for qualification. On 2026-11-07, GPU_DRIVE 55/2A delivered every RP data bit to its constrained Tang pin (27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 42, 41, 48) at 3.3 V or 0 V; a pin-identical open-flow bus-echo image echoed every address and drove 0x41 back correctly; the unchanged RTL built with Gowin EDA (diagnostic, unverified V1.9.8.11 install) reached READY with correct latch, capability and status reads. The open-flow GPU image's address-latch failure is therefore in its post-synthesis implementation, not the wiring; the Gowin build's second terminal frame exceeded the old 250 ms reply wait because its 640x480 front-to-back copy took at least about 0.8 s at 6.3 MHz (status showed busy, no faults, then completion); host reply waits now poll status. The published burst-copy Gowin image (SHA-256 55ebdfbd...) displayed and refreshed the terminal; a keyboard stall and Core 0 lockups were an RP2350 firmware Core 0 stack overflow into Core 1's 4 KiB stack bank, fixed in firmware cb2eb28, after which the user reported typing and stability working.",
  "fixed_bus_test_configuration": {
    "core_sdram_hz": 6300000,
    "physical_hdmi_pixel_hz": 25200000,
    "physical_hdmi_serializer_hz": 126000000,
    "internal_pixel_divider": 2,
    "internal_logical_scanout_hz": 3150000,
    "internal_logical_frame_hz": 7.5,
    "host_min_phase_and_setup_us": 50,
    "host_phase_only_ceiling_hz": 10000,
    "hdmi_source": "Independent constant-black 640x480/60 raster in the physical pixel domain; GPU-rendered pixels disconnected",
    "scope": "One fixed compile-time diagnostic image, not a runtime compatibility mode. Visible GPU terminal output requires a later implementation change and new qualification."
  },
